    [Test][PCP] Align MLA preprocess assertions with gate output (#19938)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    The MLA PCP regression tests added in #19800 still expect two values
    from `_mla_preprocess()`, but the mainline adaptation in #19694 extended
    its return value to `(decode, prefill, gate)`. Both CPU CI version lanes
    consequently fail, including the runs for documentation-only #18822.
    
    Update the two expected tuples to include `gate=None`. Keep the
    assertions that replicated drafts avoid PCP KV gathers and empty-owner
    ranks participate in sharded writes.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. Only two test expectations change; production code is unchanged.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Remote CPU/mock validation in an isolated Ascend container, using
    vllm-ascend base `dba1e9229` and the exact vLLM source revisions used by
    CI:
    
    | vLLM version | Before: selected regressions | After: full
    `tests/ut/attention/test_mla_v1.py` |
    | --- | --- | --- |
    | main `544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542` | Both tests failed
    with tuple-length mismatches | 214 passed |
    | v0.31.0 (`db9527a46873454610df6dbedf79a36d6bf1a7f6`) | Both tests
    failed with tuple-length mismatches | 213 passed, 1 skipped |
    
    - Command after the fix: `python -m pytest -q
    tests/ut/attention/test_mla_v1.py`.
    - Ruff 0.14.0 check/format and `git diff --check` passed.
    - Source snapshots and the fixed test file were transferred with SHA256
    verification.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
